title: FNTT & Agrarian Reform Pressure
new-page: true
view-if: ugt_agrarian_timer <= 0 and fntt_power > ugt_reformists and fntt_power > ugt_revolutionary
on-arrival: ugt_agrarian_timer = 6; month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
card-image: img/camperols.jpg
tags: ugt_affairs

= FNTT & Agrarian Reform Pressure

The *Federación Nacional de Trabajadores de la Tierra* (FNTT) has become the dominant and most militant branch of the UGT. Representing hundreds of thousands of landless day-laborers (*jornaleros*) across Andalusia, Extremadura, and La Mancha, the rural proletariat demands immediate access to the land.

With rural hunger driving impatience, the FNTT leadership insists that the Republic fulfill its promises without bureaucratic delays.

- @reform_agriculture: Direct union pressure toward the Ministry of Agriculture.
- @direct_occupations: Encourage peaceful land occupations and force government settlement.
- @strike_landlords: Organize a nationwide rural strike against landlord lockouts.
- @root: Urge the rural workers to remain patient for now.

@reform_agriculture
title: Push for Agrarian Reform in Cabinet
subtitle: Redirect to the Ministry of Agriculture's policies to accelerate legal land reform.
view-if: psoe_in_government == 1
go-to: agricultural_policy

Leveraging the large membership of the FNTT, we bring the full weight of the union to the Ministry of Agriculture, demanding immediate expropriations and IRA funding.

@direct_occupations
title: Authorize Direct Land Occupations
subtitle: Support peasant committees taking over idle fields.
on-arrival: land_reform_progress += 1; fntt_power += 2; rural_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1; polarization += 6; cnt_relation += 4; cnt_militancy += 1; js_strength += 5*(fntt_power-dissent); unemployed -= 0.1; ma_strength += 10;

Bypassing Madrid's slow legal bureaucracy, local FNTT unions march onto uncultivated fields marking out boundaries and beginning communal plowing. Unemployed peasants receive these news with joy, many of them join the FNTT and others the CNT.

@strike_landlords
title: Launch a Nationwide Agrarian Harvest Strike
subtitle: Paralyze agricultural work during peak harvest to enforce wage decrees and hiring laws.
on-arrival: fntt_power += 1; rural_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); agricultural_exports -= 0.5; unemployed += 1.2 if psoe_in_government == 0; economic_growth -= 0.2 if psoe_in_government == 1; cnt_militancy += 1; prietistas_dissent += 5; pro_republic -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1; ar_relation -= 10 if psoe_in_government == 1; prrs_relation -= 10 if psoe_in_government == 1; other_left_republicans_relation -= 10; other_right_republicans_relation -= 10; prr_relation -= 10; dlr_relation -= 10; regionalists_relation -= 10;

The FNTT calls a mass strike across southern wheat fields and olive groves to demand higher wages and better conditions.

[? if psoe_in_government == 1 : Our political allies aren't happy with this strike. ?]
[? if psoe_in_government == 0 : However; the government creates a public service to hire new peasants in substitution of the striking ones. After the failure of the Strike, large landowners refuse to re-hire the strikers, "Let them eat republic" ?]
